    // Global reference to the payment component instance
    let twoPaymentComponentInstance = null;

    // Debounce timeout for order intent
    let orderIntentDebounceTimeout = null;

    /*
     * TWO-25326 tile bugfix batch, bug 4.
     *
     * A monotonic sequence number, bumped by every intent request that actually
     * goes on the wire. A request may only publish its result — the verdict, the
     * notices, the "this company has been decided" record and the spinner coming
     * down — while it is still the newest one. It REPLACES a boolean
     * "in progress" mutex that used to sit here.
     *
     * The mutex was the reported bug, not a safeguard against it. Selecting
     * company A started a check; selecting a different company B while A's check
     * was still outstanding hit `if (inProgress) return` inside the debounce
     * callback and was DISCARDED — not queued, not retried — so B never got a
     * check at all, and the tile went on showing A's verdict. Worse, when A's
     * decision finally landed it was filed against whatever company was current
     * by then, which pinned the dedup gate to B and suppressed B's check for the
     * rest of the session even if the buyer tried again.
     *
     * Sequencing is the right shape for this: overlapping requests are allowed
     * (they are idempotent reads of a decision), and out-of-order REPLIES — the
     * thing that actually corrupts the tile — are dropped. Same guard, and the
     * same reasoning, as the one the PrestaShop plugin adopted for its own
     * order-intent leg on this ticket.
